<article class="env-definition" id="005G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/005G">Definition <span data-tag="005G">5.15.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $E \subset X$ be a subset of $X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $E$ is <em>constructible</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000034670" id="a0000034670-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> in $X$ if $E$ is a finite union of subsets of the form $U \cap V^ c$ where $U, V \subset X$ are open and retrocompact in $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $E$ is <em>locally constructible</em> in $X$ if there exists an open covering $X = \bigcup V_ i$ such that each $E \cap V_ i$ is constructible in $V_ i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>